Ladybird rejects a runtime message that reaches no listener with “Could
not establish connection. Receiving end does not exist.” MessageRouter
reports NoListener for a context with no listeners and NoReply for
listeners that decline, and ExtensionMessageBroker rejects only when no
target had a listener, or when the background page failed to start.

Chromium rejects with the same message, kReceivingEndDoesntExistError
in message_service.cc, when no receiver exists. Gecko does
the same with ERROR_NO_RECEIVERS in ExtensionParent.sys.mjs, rejecting
in recvRuntimeMessage() when raceResponses() finds no receiver. WebKit
differs: WebExtensionContext::runtimeSendMessage() completes with a
null reply when nobody responds, which resolves with undefined. Ladybird
matches Chromium and Gecko.
